  powers_starting: 2
  categories_allowed: ["Healing", "Sensitive", "Physical"]
  powers_schedule:
    - { level: 2, count: 3 }
    - { level: 3, count: 2 }
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { name: "Mathematics: Basic", bonus: 20, note: "Printed as Basic and Advanced Math (+20%); both are granted." }
    - { name: "Mathematics: Advanced", bonus: 20, note: "Printed as Basic and Advanced Math (+20%); both are granted." }
    - { name: "Radio: Basic", bonus: 15, note: "Printed as Basic Radio (+15%)." }
    - { name: "Computer Operation", bonus: 15, note: "+15% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "Biology", bonus: 10, note: "+10% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "Pathology", bonus: 10, note: "+10% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "Medical Doctor", bonus: 15, note: "+15% bonus over base." }
    - { name: "Forensics", bonus: 15, note: "Printed as Criminal Sciences and Forensics (+15%)." }
  occ_related_skills:
    count: 10
    categories:
      - { name: "Communications", bonus: 5 }
      - "Domestic"
      - "Electrical"
      - { name: "Espionage", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Medical", bonus: 10 }
      - "Physical"
      - "Pilot"
      - "Pilot Related"
      - { name: "Rogue", only: ["Streetwise"], bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Science", bonus: 5 }
      - { name: "Technical", bonus: 15 }
      - "Weapon Proficiencies"
      - "Wilderness"
    schedule: [{ level: 3, count: 3 }, { level: 6, count: 2 }, { level: 9, count: 1 }, { level: 12, count: 1 }]
    note: "Select ten other skills, plus three more at level three, two at level six and one each at levels nine and twelve. The book bars Mechanical and Military outright, so those two categories are absent rather than listed as none. HAND TO HAND IS BOUGHT FROM THIS POOL and is not granted: Basic costs one selection, Expert two, Martial Arts three and Assassin four."
  secondary_skills:
    count: 6
    note: "Six secondary skills from the same list, without the bonuses in parentheses, starting at the base skill level. The any/only/none limits above still apply."
special_abilities:
  - name: "Summon and Control Entities"
    description: "The Ghost-Maker''s signature power: summoning, or perhaps creating, energy entities. 10 I.S.P. for a haunting entity or ghost, 20 for a syphon entity, 30 for a tectonic entity, 40 for a possessing entity. Tectonic and possessing entities RESIST - they save vs psionics to break free once every minute (4 melee rounds) after being summoned - and the psychic may spend I.S.P. to worsen that save at 1 I.S.P. per -1, per attempt. Entity stats are in Rifts Conversion Book One."
  - name: "Speak with the Dead"
    description: "Summoning a haunting entity into an area carrying strong psychic residue - a crime scene, the site of a lethal accident - imprints it with the victim''s memories. The psychic can then hold a limited conversation with it, or have the ghosts re-enact what happened. A haunting entity has a very low I.Q. and is limited to the strongest emotions and memories in the area."
  - name: "Entity Combat"
    description: "A possessing or tectonic entity can be ordered to fight. If the fight could be lethal to the entity it saves to break free at +3 - and most noro would never risk the life of even a possessing entity under their control."
  - name: "Therapy and Interrogation"
    description: "A haunting entity can help a patient relive a psychological trauma, or draw out a secret the subject will not give up. The psychic must land telepathy on the subject first, then summon the entity and link the two. There is no guarantee the ghost''s impressions are what was wanted, nor whether they reflect the subject''s real past or only deep-rooted fears with no rational basis."
equipment_starting:
  - { item_id: "first-aid-kit", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "phase-tech-med-kit-full", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "hand-held-computer", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "toxic-analyzer", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "communicators-small", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "hi-10-heavy-laser-pistol", qty: 1 }
  - { item_id: "light-combat-armor", qty: 1 }
extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified against a 200 dpi render of
    printed 63, which carries the abilities, I.S.P. and bonuses. The related and
    secondary skills, equipment and money are on printed 64 and both pages were
    read to the end.
  - THE +3 SAVE VS MIND CONTROL IS NOT STORED. The book''s bonus line is "+2 to
    save vs psionics, +3 to save vs any type of mind control, and +3 to save vs
    horror factor". The sheet has a psionics save and a horror factor save and
    no mind-control save, so the psionics and horror factor figures are in
    `bonuses` and the mind-control one is here. It is a real +3 the character
    should get and the app cannot show it.
  - THE POWER SCHEDULE IS AN APPROXIMATION AND THE EXCEPTIONS ARE NOT ENFORCED.
    The book grants twelve powers outright at first level, then two picks from
    Healing/Sensitive/Physical; at second level two from those three categories
    plus ONE from Super; at third level and beyond two from ANY category. So the
    category set legitimately WIDENS with level, and `categories_allowed` is a
    single list for the whole class. It is set to the first-level three, which
    fails closed, and the level-2 Super pick is folded into the level-2 count.
    Mind wipe, psi-sword and possess others are barred at every level and
    nothing expresses that either.
  - Object Read and Possess Others are the book''s spellings; the catalog holds
    "Object Read (Psychometry)" and "Mentally Possess Others".
  - HAND TO HAND IS NOT GRANTED. Unusually, the book gives this class no hand to
    hand at all - it is bought out of the ten O.C.C. Related picks at a cost of
    one to four of them. Recorded in the related-skills note; the app has no way
    to price a skill against a pick.
  - The book''s "full medical kit (including a phase-tech med-kit)" is imported as
    a first-aid kit plus the full Phase-Tech Med Kit of printed 125. "Forensics
    kit", "sample holder" and "chemical analyzer" have no catalog rows and no
    stats in the book; the chemical analyzer is mapped to the catalog''s
    toxic-analyzer and the other two are left out rather than stubbed.
  - The sidearm and light body armour are conditional in the book - "adventurer/
    military psychics will also have" them - and are included, because a player
    character is by definition the adventuring kind.
  - Experience table transcribed from printed 183. The column is headed "Noro
    Psychic / Promethean (First Stage)"; both classes share it.
---

## Lore

All noro have psionics. An elite few develop them far past the ordinary, and the
noro produce a great many mind melters - less flashy than the mind melters of
Rifts Earth, but carrying one power nobody else has: psionic control over energy
entities.

The affinity is strongest with ghosts, the energy beings imprinted with the
personality and memories of someone dead. The Ghost-Makers can also summon and
control tectonic, syphon and even possessing entities. Many are healers and
counsellors. Others become detectives and investigators, and use their link to
the dead to solve crimes.

Noro psychics are the ones who keep their race''s crimes in front of it. A number
live full-time on Ironee, summoning ghosts to re-enact the invasion and the
self-destruction that followed. Many others serve in the CAF as officers, secret
agents, soldiers and medical officers.

## GM Notes

The O.C.C. is generally restricted to the noro race. The book leaves a door
open: another highly psionic race or individual could have an equivalent class
at the G.M.''s call, or be trained as an honorary Ghost-Maker.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'noro-psychic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'noro-psychic';

